#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:183
msgid "SourceMapConsumer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:185
msgid ""
"A SourceMapConsumer instance represents a parsed source map which we can "
"query for information about the original file positions by giving it a "
"file position in the generated source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:189
msgid "new SourceMapConsumer(rawSourceMap)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:191
msgid ""
"The only parameter is the raw source map (either as a string which can be"
" `JSON.parse`'d, or an object). According to the spec, source maps have "
"the following attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:195
msgid "`version`: Which version of the source map spec this map is following."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:197
msgid "`sources`: An array of URLs to the original source files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:199
msgid ""
"`names`: An array of identifiers which can be referenced by individual "
"mappings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:202
msgid "`sourceRoot`: Optional. The URL root from which all sources are relative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:204
msgid ""
"`sourcesContent`: Optional. An array of contents of the original source "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:206
msgid "`mappings`: A string of base64 VLQs which contain the actual mappings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:208
msgid ""
"`file`: Optional. The generated filename this source map is associated "
"with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:214
msgid "SourceMapConsumer.prototype.computeColumnSpans()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:216
msgid ""
"Compute the last column for each generated mapping. The last column is "
"inclusive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:245
msgid "SourceMapConsumer.prototype.originalPositionFor(generatedPosition)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:247
msgid ""
"Returns the original source, line, and column information for the "
"generated source's line and column positions provided. The only argument "
"is an object with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:251
msgid "`line`: The line number in the generated source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:253
msgid "`column`: The column number in the generated source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:255
msgid ""
"`bias`: Either `SourceMapConsumer.GREATEST_LOWER_BOUND` or "
"`SourceMapConsumer.LEAST_UPPER_BOUND`. Specifies whether to return the "
"closest element that is smaller than or greater than the one we are "
"searching for, respectively, if the exact element cannot be found.  "
"Defaults to `SourceMapConsumer.GREATEST_LOWER_BOUND`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:261 ../../source/source-map_README.md:300
msgid "and an object is returned with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:263
msgid ""
"`source`: The original source file, or null if this information is not "
"available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:266
msgid ""
"`line`: The line number in the original source, or null if this "
"information is not available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:269
msgid ""
"`column`: The column number in the original source, or null if this "
"information is not available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:272
msgid ""
"`name`: The original identifier, or null if this information is not "
"available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:288
msgid "SourceMapConsumer.prototype.generatedPositionFor(originalPosition)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:290
msgid ""
"Returns the generated line and column information for the original "
"source, line, and column positions provided. The only argument is an "
"object with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:294 ../../source/source-map_README.md:323
msgid "`source`: The filename of the original source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:296 ../../source/source-map_README.md:325
msgid "`line`: The line number in the original source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:298
msgid "`column`: The column number in the original source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:302 ../../source/source-map_README.md:331
msgid "`line`: The line number in the generated source, or null."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:304 ../../source/source-map_README.md:333
msgid "`column`: The column number in the generated source, or null."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:312
msgid "SourceMapConsumer.prototype.allGeneratedPositionsFor(originalPosition)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:314
msgid ""
"Returns all generated line and column information for the original "
"source, line, and column provided. If no column is provided, returns all "
"mappings corresponding to a either the line we are searching for or the "
"next closest line that has any mappings. Otherwise, returns all mappings "
"corresponding to the given line and either the column we are searching "
"for or the next closest column that has any offsets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:321
msgid "The only argument is an object with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:327
msgid "`column`: Optional. The column number in the original source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:329
msgid "and an array of objects is returned, each with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:345
msgid "SourceMapConsumer.prototype.hasContentsOfAllSources()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:347
msgid ""
"Return true if we have the embedded source content for every source "
"listed in the source map, false otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:350
msgid ""
"In other words, if this method returns `true`, then "
"`consumer.sourceContentFor(s)` will succeed for every source `s` in "
"`consumer.sources`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:364
msgid ""
"SourceMapConsumer.prototype.sourceContentFor(source[, "
"returnNullOnMissing])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:366
msgid ""
"Returns the original source content for the source provided. The only "
"argument is the URL of the original source file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:369
msgid ""
"If the source content for the given source is not found, then an error is"
" thrown. Optionally, pass `true` as the second param to have `null` "
"returned instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:387
msgid "SourceMapConsumer.prototype.eachMapping(callback, context, order)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:389
msgid ""
"Iterate over each mapping between an original source/line/column and a "
"generated line/column in this source map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:392
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`callback`: The function that is called with each mapping. Mappings have "
"the form `{ source, generatedLine, generatedColumn, originalLine, "
"originalColumn, name }`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:396
msgid ""
"`context`: Optional. If specified, this object will be the value of "
"`this` every time that `callback` is called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:399
msgid ""
"`order`: Either `SourceMapConsumer.GENERATED_ORDER` or "
"`SourceMapConsumer.ORIGINAL_ORDER`. Specifies whether you want to iterate"
" over the mappings sorted by the generated file's line/column order or "
"the original's source/line/column order, respectively. Defaults to "
"`SourceMapConsumer.GENERATED_ORDER`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:422
msgid "SourceMapGenerator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:424
msgid ""
"An instance of the SourceMapGenerator represents a source map which is "
"being built incrementally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:427
msgid "new SourceMapGenerator([startOfSourceMap])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:429
msgid "You may pass an object with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:431
msgid ""
"`file`: The filename of the generated source that this source map is "
"associated with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:434
msgid "`sourceRoot`: A root for all relative URLs in this source map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:436
msgid ""
"`skipValidation`: Optional. When `true`, disables validation of mappings "
"as they are added. This can improve performance but should be used with "
"discretion, as a last resort. Even then, one should avoid using this flag"
" when running tests, if possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:448
msgid "SourceMapGenerator.fromSourceMap(sourceMapConsumer)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:450
msgid ""
"Creates a new `SourceMapGenerator` from an existing `SourceMapConsumer` "
"instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:452
msgid "`sourceMapConsumer` The SourceMap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:458
msgid "SourceMapGenerator.prototype.addMapping(mapping)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:460
msgid ""
"Add a single mapping from original source line and column to the "
"generated source's line and column for this source map being created. The"
" mapping object should have the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:464
msgid "`generated`: An object with the generated line and column positions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:466
msgid "`original`: An object with the original line and column positions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:468
msgid "`source`: The original source file (relative to the sourceRoot)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:470
msgid "`name`: An optional original token name for this mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:480
msgid "SourceMapGenerator.prototype.setSourceContent(sourceFile, sourceContent)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:482
msgid "Set the source content for an original source file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:484
msgid "`sourceFile` the URL of the original source file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:486
msgid "`sourceContent` the content of the source file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:493
msgid ""
"SourceMapGenerator.prototype.applySourceMap(sourceMapConsumer[, "
"sourceFile[, sourceMapPath]])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:495
msgid ""
"Applies a SourceMap for a source file to the SourceMap. Each mapping to "
"the supplied source file is rewritten using the supplied SourceMap. Note:"
" The resolution for the resulting mappings is the minimum of this map and"
" the supplied map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:500
msgid "`sourceMapConsumer`: The SourceMap to be applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:502
msgid ""
"`sourceFile`: Optional. The filename of the source file. If omitted, "
"sourceMapConsumer.file will be used, if it exists. Otherwise an error "
"will be thrown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:506
msgid ""
"`sourceMapPath`: Optional. The dirname of the path to the SourceMap to be"
" applied. If relative, it is relative to the SourceMap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:509
msgid ""
"This parameter is needed when the two SourceMaps aren't in the same "
"directory, and the SourceMap to be applied contains relative source "
"paths. If so, those relative source paths need to be rewritten relative "
"to the SourceMap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:514
msgid ""
"If omitted, it is assumed that both SourceMaps are in the same directory,"
" thus not needing any rewriting. (Supplying `'.'` has the same effect.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:517
msgid "SourceMapGenerator.prototype.toString()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:519
msgid "Renders the source map being generated to a string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:526
msgid "SourceNode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:528
msgid ""
"SourceNodes provide a way to abstract over interpolating and/or "
"concatenating snippets of generated JavaScript source code, while "
"maintaining the line and column information associated between those "
"snippets and the original source code. This is useful as the final "
"intermediate representation a compiler might use before outputting the "
"generated JS and source map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:534
msgid "new SourceNode([line, column, source[, chunk[, name]]])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:536
msgid ""
"`line`: The original line number associated with this source node, or "
"null if it isn't associated with an original line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:539
msgid ""
"`column`: The original column number associated with this source node, or"
" null if it isn't associated with an original column."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:542
msgid "`source`: The original source's filename; null if no filename is provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:544
msgid ""
"`chunk`: Optional. Is immediately passed to `SourceNode.prototype.add`, "
"see below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:547
msgid "`name`: Optional. The original identifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:557
msgid ""
"SourceNode.fromStringWithSourceMap(code, sourceMapConsumer[, "
"relativePath])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:559
msgid "Creates a SourceNode from generated code and a SourceMapConsumer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:561
msgid "`code`: The generated code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:563
msgid "`sourceMapConsumer` The SourceMap for the generated code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:565
msgid ""
"`relativePath` The optional path that relative sources in "
"`sourceMapConsumer` should be relative to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:574
msgid "SourceNode.prototype.add(chunk)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:576
msgid "Add a chunk of generated JS to this source node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:578 ../../source/source-map_README.md:591
msgid ""
"`chunk`: A string snippet of generated JS code, another instance of  "
"`SourceNode`, or an array where each member is one of those things."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:587
msgid "SourceNode.prototype.prepend(chunk)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:589
msgid "Prepend a chunk of generated JS to this source node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:598
msgid "SourceNode.prototype.setSourceContent(sourceFile, sourceContent)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:600
msgid ""
"Set the source content for a source file. This will be added to the "
"`SourceMap` in the `sourcesContent` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:603
msgid "`sourceFile`: The filename of the source file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:605
msgid "`sourceContent`: The content of the source file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:612
msgid "SourceNode.prototype.walk(fn)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:614
msgid ""
"Walk over the tree of JS snippets in this node and its children. The "
"walking function is called once for each snippet of JS and is passed that"
" snippet and the its original associated source's line/column location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:618 ../../source/source-map_README.md:642
msgid "`fn`: The traversal function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:637
msgid "SourceNode.prototype.walkSourceContents(fn)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:639
msgid ""
"Walk over the tree of SourceNodes. The walking function is called for "
"each source file content and is passed the filename and source content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:659
msgid "SourceNode.prototype.join(sep)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:661
msgid ""
"Like `Array.prototype.join` except for SourceNodes. Inserts the separator"
" between each of this source node's children."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:664
msgid "`sep`: The separator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:675
msgid "SourceNode.prototype.replaceRight(pattern, replacement)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:677
msgid ""
"Call `String.prototype.replace` on the very right-most source snippet. "
"Useful for trimming white space from the end of a source node, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:680
msgid "`pattern`: The pattern to replace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:682
msgid "`replacement`: The thing to replace the pattern with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:689
msgid "SourceNode.prototype.toString()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:691
msgid ""
"Return the string representation of this source node. Walks over the tree"
" and concatenates all the various snippets together to one string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:708
msgid "SourceNode.prototype.toStringWithSourceMap([startOfSourceMap])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:710
msgid ""
"Returns the string representation of this tree of source nodes, plus a "
"SourceMapGenerator which contains all the mappings between the generated "
"and original sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map_README.md:714
msgid "The arguments are the same as those to `new SourceMapGenerator`."
msgstr ""

